{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":891,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Prov.4","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Proverbs","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Proverbs 4","reference":"Proverbs 4","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"An exhortation to the study of wisdom, is forced by various arguments, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-13.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"A caution against bad company, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"14-19.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Directions for the attaining and keeping of wisdom, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"20-27.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"A father - Of me, who have paternal authority over you and affection for you.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":10,"text":"Tender - Young and tender in years, and tenderly educated.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":11,"text":"Only beloved - Beloved above all the rest.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":13,"text":"Said - The following verses, at least as far as the tenth verse, are the words of David.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":15,"text":"With all - Even with the price of all.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":16,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":17,"text":"Exalt - Let her have thine highest esteem and affection.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":18,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":19,"text":"Grace - A beautiful ornament, such as they used to put upon their heads.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":20,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":21,"text":"For - They cannot sleep with quietness.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":22,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":23,"text":"For - Wickedness is as pleasant to them as their bread.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":24,"text":"18.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":25,"text":"But - Just men daily grow in knowledge, and grace, and consolation, 'till all be perfected and swallowed up in glory.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":26,"text":"19.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":27,"text":"Darkness - Full of ignorance and error, of uncertainty and confusion, of danger and misery.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":28,"text":"23.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":29,"text":"Heart - Thy thoughts, will, and affections.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":30,"text":"For - From thence proceed all the actions, as of the natural, so of the spiritual life, which lead to eternal life.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":31,"text":"24.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":32,"text":"Mouth - All sorts of sinful words.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":33,"text":"25.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":34,"text":"Right on - Direct all thine actions to a right end, and keep thy mind fixed upon that way which leads to it, and neither look or turn aside to the right-hand or the left.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":35,"text":"26.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":36,"text":"Ponder - Consider thine actions before thou dost them, and see that they agree with the rule.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":37,"text":"And - Let thine actions be uniformly and constantly good in spite of all temptations.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":4}}